This was my first spork ascention. I had played a bit more than a
handful of spork games, and the furthest I had gotten was around
medusa. I had little spoilage of spork details, apart from the
intrinsic and genocide system, and that alchemy didn't work like in
vanilla. Oh, and I had the vague notion that Vlad had a level draining
weapon.

My barbarian was a lucky one, as he found 2 early magic lamps (one for
light, one failed to give a wish) and a random (I think it was random,
I found a couple of bones, but by context I figure it was random) wand
of wishing at 1:3. I wished for 2?ocharging, Master key of thievery,
+2 Grayswandir and (after doing soko for Boh), a +2 SDSM. Since I
identified ?oGeno and had found 3 magic markers, I did some extensive
genocide: I genoed Master Lich, Arch lich, Master mind flayer, mind
flayer, disenchanters and much later hill giant shaman and L [yes, i
spent 3 ?Geno with L, while I could have done it with 2, but I was not
sure of the algorithm].
Much later I would also wish for a +2[oMR and some +2 speed boots. The
SB I had from early game were destroyed by a demi-Lich, to my great
surprise, since I had MR. Apparently the deteriorate armor spell can
destroy deteriorated armor? After that I fixed all my armor, except
for SDSM (not sure if that can be deteriorated or not, also not sure
if 'fixed' prevents deteriorantion). Also wasted a wish on helm of
brilliance to see if I could cast Identify and remove curse: I
couldn't even with robe and high stats.

I also found some interesting new armor. A shield of light, gauntlets
of force and gauntlets of fortune. As for the shield of light, I
enchanted it to +4, in hopes of it giving a high light radius. As I
found out with my wasted ?oEA, that is not the case, so a shield of
light always ends up giving less light than a magic lamp. Also, since
I used the 2-handed lifestealer a lot, I ended up not using the shield
at all on the ascension run: it was just a waste of ?EA.
I though that gauntlets of force was gauntlets of power nerfed, so I
also enchanted it in hopes of gaining something. As nothing changed I
searched a bit and it apparently only gives bonuses to bare-handed
attack. Another waste of ?oEA.
Finally, I though the gauntlets of fortune was like a luckstone, but
with enchantment bonuses (even if capped). Since I had a blessed
luckstone and luck more or less maxed, I didn't use it at all. Bad
choice, apparently, since I searched a bit and it seems the GFortune
are just like a luckstone but with +5 to baseluck instead of +3. Also
not sure if it allows to get to +15 luck.

On my previous spork games I already had found out that sacrificing
for gifts sucks in spork. Okay, some highly enchanted boots or gloves
might have been nice, but receiving plate armor when already using
mithril (or maybe SDSM, don't remember for sure) sucks. I pity the
spork-magic-bane-deprived wizards (yes, still the first _artifact_
gift, but some games I did not receive artifacts at all).

Another surprise was the thoughness of monsters, even with enchanted
graywsandir. And their attack, also. Around medusa level I found an
Angel (I think so, at least it was a white A), which appeared on
warning as a 5. It hit HARD. It would NOT die. I run away and come
back. I put on =oRegeneration. I had the freaking master key of
thievery (still half physical damage?). At last, I got a lucky roll
and managed to not die, while still getting sufficiently low HP to get
fully restored with prayer. Other A didn't give the same trouble, but
by then I had +7 lifestealer and better AC. Oh, and did I mention that
the better monster AC means that /oDeath are much harder kill Rodney?
As for Vlad, I think it was a good idea to buff him up. But giving him
life stealer?? A bit to much, IMO, as I would only fight him with a
level draining resistance or (as was the case) a rubber chicken.

On final preparations I did some alchemy testing, as I did not want to
waste potions badly. So, for the record:
-alchemising diluted potions do not give water potions (yey);
-diluted !o[EF]Healing give half HP maximum raise (so it's not worth
to alchemise !oEA to !oFH for that purpose);
-after a while (didn't notice when, somewhere between 200HP and
250HP?) the potions only raise max HP by one, so keep them for getting
healed: you'll need it on astral.

Eventually I reached astral, and it was though, even with ~ -40AC, +7
lifestealer and master key of thievery. I had a LOAD of /oTeleport
(are they spawned more often in spork? if so, thanks, Derek), though,
and enough !oFH. For an extra bit of trial, the correct altar HAD to
be the 3rd one: Death's.
